WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.729
Now, Republicans have been saying the inspector
general is investigating the Russia probe.

00:00:05.729 --> 00:00:11.809
When that report comes out, you will see how
the entire Russia probe was a completely inappropriate

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:18.539
witch hunt, inappropriately run, uh, and also
based on political bias and the Trump, Ian

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:21.449
Wright has had a lot riding on this for awhile.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:25.529
They've put a lot of eggs in this office of
the inspector general report.

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:32.210
Uh, and yesterday the office of the inspector
general published the report and it says that

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:37.960
the Russia probe was done in total correctly
with proper limits carried out in the right

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.530
way without political bias.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.950
Now they did find some specific procedural
pieces that were problematic, which I will

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.950
tell you about.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.640
I have no interest in hiding that from you,
but certainly not the bombshell that Republicans

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.110
and Trumpists were promising.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.110
So let's go through it.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.360
The report is more than 400 pages.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.340
The highlights include that the FBI had a
quote authorized purpose when it started its

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.340
investigation.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.930
The investigation was not opened because of
political animus from the FBI against Donald

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:07.930
Trump.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.140
Informants were not used in violation of the
FBI's rules, so it's a clean bill of health

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.340
for the investigation with a few elements
of a wrongdoing.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.340
What were those elements?

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.250
Well, the report says that once the inventor
investigation got going, they believe the

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:33.130
FBI would sometimes emphasize information
that made Trump look bad and downplay information

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.040
that made Trump look good.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.580
Now remember, this is still an office that
is not without political bias, but let's grant

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.580
it to them.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.200
Because the entire structure and framework
of the investigation has been vindicated.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.440
I'm fine granting that.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.470
Maybe that is something that took place.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.460
Here's an excerpt from the report regarding
another area of controversy, which is that

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.720
the surveillance of Carter page specifically
was heavily based on the steel dossier.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.070
The FBI request form drew almost entirely
from Steele's reporting in describing the

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:09.940
factual basis to establish, establish probable
cause, to believe that Carter page was an

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.950
agent of a foreign power.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:15.590
Now again, I say let's just accept the criticism
and move on.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.590
Let them have it.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:22.940
Let them have the critique that specifically
the surveillance of Carter page was too heavily

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.480
based on the Steele dossier.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.380
It's a sliver of this entire thing.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.550
Let them have it.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.740
Bearing in mind of course, that lots of that
Steele dossier was later corroborated.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:39.200
Now, Donald Trump's attorney general henchman
William Barr disagrees with the report.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.700
That probably doesn't surprise you.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.730
He believes that the report, uh, is just flat
out wrong.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.600
Of course, that it should have been much more
um, uh, critical of the way the investigation

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.600
was carried out.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.600
So big picture.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.950
I don't know how much time we need to spend
on this.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.010
Both sides are claiming victory.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:01.100
Democrats claim the report completely exonerates
the way the investigation was carried out,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.850
Republicans claim that it's devastating.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:09.710
The reality is the report is mostly exculpatory
of the FBI's investigation into Donald Trump

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:14.650
and Russia in any huge long investigation
like this.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.550
It's not shocking that there were a few procedural
issues that the report was able to find my

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.550
guesses.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:27.410
If you do this deep of an investigation into
any major government investigation, you would

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:33.820
find some items that at this level of granularity
could have been better handled.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.390
That is not hugely surprising to me.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.340
It doesn't excuse anything, but it's not hugely
surprising.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.810
What you have to remember is Republicans hyped
this report to Helen back and other than being

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:48.060
able to say, well, the Carter page surveillance
was based too heavily on the Steele dossier.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:53.050
FBI officials played up certain things unfairly
to Trump once it got going.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.350
That's all they have.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:04:00.220
They are almost better off ignoring the report
altogether rather than pretend that it's devastating

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.220
to the Russia probe because it's not.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:08.069
And what we have to do is ensure that we don't
allow the report to be misrepresented.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:12.500
This is a totally unsurprising conclusion
to the report.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.900
It's good that it's done.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.840
We can now try to start moving on from this
talking point from Republicans who have been

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:25.440
saying, just you wait until that OIG report
destroys this an entire investigation that's

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.440
over.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:05:10.520
Let's just make sure we don't let them continue
the false

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:48.910
talking points.

